      "status_notes": "GHSA-35pj-rg5r-8rpv: when the first daemon of a Gradle version started, Gradle created the daemon registry (registry.bin) and its directory with default permissions and restricted them only afterwards, so another local user could open the file in that window and keep reading the daemon tokens written to it later. Gradle 8.14.7 and earlier 8.x releases are affected and 8.14.8 carries the fix (https://github.com/gradle/gradle/security/advisories/GHSA-35pj-rg5r-8rpv, fix commit https://github.com/gradle/gradle/commit/7eec04196b9e911a2be6186146ac009e9c2a1e74, in https://github.com/gradle/gradle/compare/v8.14.7...v8.14.8). The DHI gradle-8 package is Gradle built from the upstream v8.14.x source tag, and the gradle-*.jar files in /usr/share/java/gradle/lib of each build carry that version: 8.14.4 in 8.14.4-r0 to 8.14.4-r3, 8.14.5 in 8.14.5-r3 to 8.14.5-r9, 8.14.6 in 8.14.6-r0 to 8.14.6-r2, 8.14.7 in 8.14.7-r0 and 8.14.8 in 8.14.8-r0. We read every published gradle-8 package for Alpine 3.23 in the DHI Alpine repository as listed in its index on 2026-11-26 (16 versions, 8.14.4-r0 to 8.14.8-r0), after checking each package against its index checksum; the aarch64 package of each version has the same index checksum as the x86_64 one, and 8.14.5-r4 is published for x86_64 only. We opened every jar in each package, nested jars included. The fix adds org.gradle.internal.file.nio.OwnerOnlyFiles (gradle-files) and makes DaemonDir (gradle-daemon-protocol) create the registry directory through it with owner-only permissions. OwnerOnlyFiles is present, and DaemonDir uses it, in 8.14.8-r0 only. The range ends at 8.14.8-r0, the first build with Gradle 8.14.8."
    },
